From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:21:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] capture late pytest exit stacks for derived-session
 investigation

The derived-session test has twice printed all three passes before the
600-second per-file timeout. Quiet, GC-pressure and bounded concurrent
replays have not reproduced the original hang, so this is diagnostics,
NOT a deflake or a claim that the root cause is known.

Load a minimal plugin before capture only for that test file. Preserve an
original stderr descriptor and rearm a C faulthandler watchdog after pytest
unconfigure so atexit and interpreter-finalization stacks reach the runner.
Log phase markers without logging locks. Record child status before killing
a timeout: communicate can wait on inherited stdout after the child exits.
Leave deadlines, retries, cleanup and exit statuses unchanged.

Proof: canonical runner passes original tests, synthetic real atexit and
finalization stack transport, pass/fail exit preservation, real forkserver
success/poll, scoped injection, pre-kill status, and runner regression suites.
Removing teardown rearm makes both synthetic transport cases fail (RED).
Full scripts/check --base HEAD passes. The original historical failure
still needs a natural stack followed by a causal fix and red/base proof.
